    "description": "I am a 31-year old professional woman, born and raised in San Francisco. I enjoy world traveling, dancing, cooking, hosting events, theatrical arts, and film. I love my city and do a lot of work with various local non-profits and small businesses. I know this city like the back of my hand. I truly value and enjoy this house. I seek a responsible, similarly aged and like-minded person with whom to share it. The house is located on the borderline of Silverview Terrace and Bayview District in a quiet and safe location. Transportation is plentiful, but there is a garage for parking if you have a car. This house is perfect for a busy professional who is \"social\" but wants a nice place to chill when they get home. A place that actually FEELS like home.The home features:2 bedrooms (1 for you and 1 for me), a living room, and an additional room that can be used as an office or potentially a 3rd bedroom1 bathroom with separate tub and showerLarge Gourmet kitchen with dishwasherEnclosed garage + storage Internet access/cable readyIn home washer/dryerHuge backyard that needs some work and I plan on spending a lot of time fixing it up. You are welcome to join! Super cute cat named Beba who minds her mannersNearest Transportation:8ax, 9T-Third54 Felton24 Divisadero44 O'Shaughnessy23 MontereyGlen Park Bart StationEasy freeway access (Oakland, Silicon Valley, and Walnut Creek)29 SunsetThe Fine Print:Rent is $1600PG&E and Comcast are split evenly and are additional each month - I've got water and garbage coveredA $300 deposit + $100 (towards setting up the internet and cable) is required, moving you in at a total of $2,000The home is available October 1st, 2014 with a 1-year lease (possibility of longer term)All candidates must be wiling to show proof of incomeNo cigarettes in the house, but I am 420 friendlySerious inquiries only... No \"BS\"Happy house hunting! I know it's hard out there!Water + Garbage Covered."
